  [RISK] drivers/mailbox/riscv-sbi-mpxy-mbox.c:400-472  mpxy_mbox_send_rpmi_data
      The SEND_WITHOUT_RESPONSE case (lines 453-467) validates only buffer non-NULL/length consistency and channel capability flags. No integrity attestation, nonce verification, HMAC, or cryptographic binding exists on the outbound message path. Any service group -- including a future BOOTSTATUS -- using this dispatch would deliver AP-supplied data to the PmC unauthenticated. Currently safe only because no RPMI_SRVGRP_BOOTSTATUS service group is defined and no BOOTSTATUS driver exists; the invariant 'no security-sensitive service groups will be added without attestation infrastructure' is not enforced in code.
  [RISK] drivers/mailbox/riscv-sbi-mpxy-mbox.c:275-297  mpxy_send_message_without_resp
      Direct memcpy of AP-supplied data into SBI shared memory followed by bare SBI_EXT_MPXY_SEND_MSG_WITHOUT_RESP ecall. No attestation token, HMAC, or session binding is constructed or transmitted. The fire-and-forget semantics (no response expected) mean the sender receives no acknowledgement and injection is undetectable by the AP. This is the exact transport a BOOTSTATUS_SET_STATUS service would use. Currently safe only because no caller submits BOOTSTATUS messages; there is no code-level barrier preventing such use.
  [RISK] include/linux/mailbox/riscv-rpmi-message.h:207-220  rpmi_mbox_init_send_without_response
